## Why This Question Is Asked
This question evaluates real-world multi-region MLOps expertise, covering data privacy, residency requirements, and cost controls. It tests the ability to design end-to-end pipelines and implement risk mitigation strategies.

## Key Concepts
- Vertex AI canary rollout and per-region feature stores
- Data residency controls and privacy-preserving preprocessing
- Drift and latency monitoring with automated alerting
- Cost governance through budgets and quotas
- Model rollback procedures and criteria

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo-pipeline wiring for Vertex AI
const { PipelineServiceClient } = require('@google-cloud/aiplatform');

async function createCanaryPipeline() {
  const client = new PipelineServiceClient({ apiEndpoint: 'us-central1-aiplatform.googleapis.com' });

  const [job] = await client.createPipelineJob({
    parent: `projects/${PROJECT}/locations/${REGION}`,
    pipelineJob: {
      displayName: 'av-sensing-canary-pipeline',
      pipelineSpec: {
        pipelineRoot: `gs://${BUCKET}/pipeline_root/${PIPELINE_ID}`,
        components: {
          preprocessingComponent,
          featureStoreComponent,
          trainingComponent,
          deploymentComponent
        }
      },
      // Canary deployment config
      deploymentConfig: {
        trafficRouting: {
          canary: { 
            percentage: 10,
            routes: [{ weight: 10, endpoint: 'canary' }] 
          }
        },
        // Cross-region residency
        reservedRanges: ['us-east1', 'us-west1', 'europe-west4']
      }
    }
  });
}

// Monitor for rollback criteria
async function checkRollbackConditions(modelId) {
  const monitoringClient = new ModelMonitoringServiceClient();
  const [stats] = await monitoringClient.getStats({
    name: `projects/${PROJECT}/models/${modelId}/stats`
  });

  const conditions = [
    { metric: 'latency', threshold: 150, actual: stats.predictionLatency.p99 },
    { metric: 'drift', threshold: 0.1, actual: stats.featureDrift.jensenShannon },
    { metric: 'errorRate', threshold: 0.01, actual: stats.errorRate }
  ];

  const shouldRollback = conditions.some(c => c.actual > c.threshold);
  if (shouldRollback) {
    await triggerRollback(modelId);
  }
}
```

## Why This Is Asked

Tests a candidate's ability to design a compliant, language-agnostic text classification pipeline using Vertex AI, Dataflow, and Pub/Sub, with privacy safeguards and practical operational concerns.

## Key Concepts

- Dataflow-based redaction and translation for multilingual content
- End-to-end data lineage: storage of raw and processed text
- Weekly Vertex AI training with canary deployment
- Drift and latency monitoring with rollback strategy
- Practical cost considerations: storage, translation, training, and serving

## Code Example

